<script>
  import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.pulse';
  import Footer from '../../components/Footer.pulse';

  let title = "Pulse v0.15.0 Released";
  let subtitle = "The Performance Update: 5x Smaller Runtime, Reactivity V2, and Beautiful Errors.";
  let date = "February 6, 2026";
</script>

<Navbar />

<main class="page">
  <div class="content">
    <div class="header">
      <span class="date">{date}</span>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">{subtitle}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="body">
      <p>
        We are thrilled to announce <strong>Pulse v0.15.0</strong>, a major milestone in our journey to build the ultimate LLM-native web framework. This release focuses on massive performance gains, runtime optimization, and developer experience.
      </p>

      <h2>⚡ 5x Smaller Runtime</h2>
      <p>
        We've completely rewritten the core runtime. The new <strong>Functional Runtime</strong> drops class-based overhead in favor of tree-shakable functions.
      </p>
      <div class="highlight-box">
        <strong>Runtime Size Comparison (gzip):</strong>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>v0.14:</strong> ~20kB</li>
          <li><strong>v0.15:</strong> <strong>~4kB</strong></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>🧬 Reactivity V2</h2>
      <p>
        The reactivity engine is now strictly dependency-tracking.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Auto-Tracking:</strong> No need for manual dependency arrays.</li>
        <li><strong>Smart Scheduler:</strong> Updates are batched and scheduled via microtasks, ensuring zero unnecessary re-renders.</li>
        <li><strong>Memory Efficient:</strong> Signals and effects are now plain objects/closures, reducing memory pressure.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>🖼️ Template Cloning DOM</h2>
      <p>
        We've ditched <code>document.createElement</code> chains for standard HTML <code>&lt;template&gt;</code> cloning.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Instantiation:</strong> Cloning a template content is up to <strong>10x faster</strong> than creating elements one by one.</li>
        <li><strong>Path Walking:</strong> We locate nodes using pre-computed integer paths (e.g. <code>firstChild.nextSibling</code>), bypassing slow CSS selectors entirely.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>🤖 LLM Introspective</h2>
      <p>
        Pulse v0.15 is designed to be understood by AI.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Component Introspector:</strong> Generates deterministic Semantic Models of your code.</li>
        <li><strong>Agent Friendly:</strong> Agents can confidently refactor Pulse components because the framework structure is strictly typed and validatable.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>💅 Beautiful Errors</h2>
      <p>
        We believe errors should be helpful, not scary. The new Error Overlay features:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Glassmorphism Design:</strong> A modern, dark-themed UI.</li>
        <li><strong>Smart Suggestions:</strong> AI-driven hints to fix the problem instantly.</li>
        <li><strong>Clean Stack Traces:</strong> Noise reduction to focus on your code.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>v0.14 vs v0.15 Comparison</h2>
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Feature</th>
              <th>v0.14</th>
              <th>v0.15 (Current)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Runtime Size</strong></td>
              <td>~20kB</td>
              <td><strong>~4kB</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Reactivity</strong></td>
              <td>Class-based</td>
              <td><strong>Functional</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>DOM Engine</strong></td>
              <td>createElement</td>
              <td><strong>Template Cloning</strong></td>
            </tr>
             <tr>
              <td><strong>Error UI</strong></td>
              <td>Standard</td>
              <td><strong>Premium Glass</strong></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        Phase 6 (Cleanup) is complete. Our next focus is <strong>Ecosystem Growth</strong>—expect a router, state management patterns, and more "Magical primitives" in v0.16!
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<Footer />

